  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="HHFF9F4E3640A578CDF5DE55A091A9A0F9" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4"></ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pikka Transportation Company is subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements generally conform to those required by FERC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE 1.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BALANCE SHEET&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At June 30, 2026 the provision for the asset retirement obligation for Pikka Transportation Company, LLC was $15,418,098. The provision has been estimated using existing technology, at current prices, and is expected to be incurred through the end of life of the pipeline. While the provision is based on the best estimate of future costs and the economic lives of the pipeline, there is uncertainty regarding both the amount and timing of incurring these costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE 2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE 3&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE 4&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE 5&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pikka Pipeline is a 22 mile, 16-inch diameter hydrocarbon liquids pipeline from an origin point at the Nanushuk Processing Facility located at the east end of the Pikka Unit in the North Slope Borough of Alaska, to a destination point at the connection of the Pikka Pipeline with the Kuparuk Sales Oil Pipeline, also in the North Slope Borough of Alaska. Pipeline construction was completed in mid-2025, and first oil was received into the pipeline in May of 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE 6&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
